<http://data.silknow.org/object/da6c3c32-d48d-3c39-89d8-e5588f613ea8/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "MAN'S CLOAK\n1874\nThe cloak is displayed to show the back. It is made from two lengths of fabric joined to make a horizontal seam around the middle of the garment. The tapestry-woven fabric is very decorative, but to add further visual interest it has been given a watered, or moiré, effect. This was done by pressing the cloth under heavy weights to flatten some of the ribs of the weave, leaving others unaltered so that they reflect the light differently.\nTapestry-woven silk, with gilded metal threads and a watered effect.\nIran, Kashan [2006]"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/da6c3c32-d48d-3c39-89d8-e5588f613ea8> .

